WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.927
Welcome to Module 7, Advanced Python Techniques.

00:00:04.927 --> 00:00:10.857
Up to this point, we have spent a lot of time building a strong foundation in Python.

00:00:10.857 --> 00:00:17.257
We have worked with variables, conditions, loops, functions, data structures, and ways to organize our code.

00:00:17.257 --> 00:00:23.742
In this module, we are going to take some of those ideas and look at more compact and

00:00:23.742 --> 00:00:27.852
more powerful ways to write Python.

00:00:27.852 --> 00:00:32.777
You will see techniques such as list comprehensions, lambda functions, and generators.

00:00:32.777 --> 00:00:38.992
We will also spend some time on debugging and code efficiency.

00:00:38.992 --> 00:00:42.037
I want to emphasize something from the beginning.

00:00:42.037 --> 00:00:47.687
Advanced Python does not necessarily mean writing the shortest code possible.

00:00:47.687 --> 00:00:51.982
Short code can sometimes become difficult to understand.

00:00:51.982 --> 00:00:59.117
Our goal is to write code that is clear, useful, and appropriate for the problem we are solving.

00:00:59.117 --> 00:01:06.707
These techniques are especially helpful in analytics because we often need to filter values, transform data,

00:01:06.707 --> 00:01:10.372
sort records, or process large collections.

00:01:10.372 --> 00:01:15.897
As we move through the examples, try to focus less on memorizing the syntax and more on understanding

00:01:15.897 --> 00:01:20.320
what each technique is helping us accomplish.
